927"} "Paul Elvstrøm"] " of Denmark won his fourth consecutive gold medal in one-person dinghy, making him the first Olympian to win the same event at four straight Olympics, although some purists demur because the 1948 event was held in the Firefly class. Elvstrøm’s feat has only been equalled by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78857"} "Al Oerter"] " in athletics in the discus throw (1956-68) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78692"} "Carl Lewis"] " in athletics in the long jump (1984-96). In Roma Elvstrøm had three firsts and a second in the first six races, and sat out the last race, not needing a score to win his gold medal. Bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/63117"} "André Nelis"] " of Belgium had been the silver medalist in 1956."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/61927"} "Paul Elvstrøm"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} "8,171"] [:td {} "1,645 (1)"] [:td {} "946 (5)"] [:td {} "1,645 (1)"] [:td {} "1,344 (2)"] [:td {} "946 (5)"] [:td {} "1,645 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/63878"} "Aleksander Tšutšelov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "6,520"] [:td {} "800 (7)"] [:td {} "1,645 (1)"] [:td {} "1,344 (2)"] [:td {} "645 (10)"] [:td {} "415 (17)"] [:td {} "1,344 (2)"] [:td {} "742 (8)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"}